# Everything under data/ is runtime state, and some of it is secret:
#   users.json    scrypt hashes + salts  (0600, but never commit it)
#   sessions.json hashed session tokens
#   audit.jsonl   who called what, when
#   history.json  several MB of time series, rewritten every 2 minutes
/data/
/*.log
*.tmp

config/local.json
# The dated backups scripts/setup.js keeps when it replaces local.json (2026-09-16, audit I5):
# they hold the same RPC password, so they must never be one `git add` away from a commit.
config/*.bak-*
# Display settings, written by the app itself (POST /api/settings). THIS DEPLOYMENT's
# preferences, not the shipped ones -- those are DEFAULTS in public/js/settings.js and
# belong in the repository. Ignored for the same reason local.json is: it is a choice
# someone made on one machine.
config/blockyard.json

node_modules/
.DS_Store
._*
*.swp

# local agent worktrees and settings
.claude/

# working notes stay on the working machine (never published)
worklog/
docs/STATE-*.md
# scoping reports and proposals that are not decisions yet
docs/PRIVATE-*.md
